  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In Circuit-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> and Circuit-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;shown in the figures, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></math>.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are the power dissipations in Circuit-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and Circuit-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;when the switches <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are in open conditions, respectively.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are the power dissipations in Circuit-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> and Circuit-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> when the switches <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are in closed conditions, respectively.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0000_610b6baecde3.png\" style=\"width: 375px; height: 300px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>Which of the following statement(s) is(are) correct?</p>"
